      "text": "Registration – SMI\n Contact Us\n Contact Us\n Sign In\n Register\n Home\nAbout\n President’s Message\n Executive Officers and Board\n Past Presidents\n Staff List\n Privacy Policy\nMember Benefits\n Affinity Programs\n SMI Scholarship Program\n Springs Advice\n Regulatory Compliance\n Find a Springmaker\n Find a Supplier\nIssues\nSprings Magazine\n Issues\n Springs Magazine Media Kit\n Space Reservation Request\n Ad Submission\n Editorial Submission\nEvents\n Event Calendar\n Spring Design Training Program\n Annual Meeting\n SpringWorld\nOnline Store\nMembership\n Benefits of Membership\n Member Search\n Apply For Membership\n My account\nLogin\n Serving, supporting and educating North American precision spring manufacturers in their pursuit of competitiveness in world markets.\n Member Login\n Home\nAbout\n President’s Message\n Executive Officers and Board\n Past Presidents\n Staff List\n Privacy Policy\nMember Benefits\n Affinity Programs\n SMI Scholarship Program\n Springs Advice\n Regulatory Compliance\n Find a Springmaker\n Find a Supplier\nIssues\nSprings Magazine\n Issues\n Springs Magazine Media Kit\n Space Reservation Request\n Ad Submission\n Editorial Submission\nEvents\n Event Calendar\n Spring Design Training Program\n Annual Meeting\n SpringWorld\nOnline Store\nMembership\n Benefits of Membership\n Member Search\n Apply For Membership\n My account\nLogin\n Apply For Membership\n Please complete the application and a member of SMI’s staff will contact you.\nPlease select the membership type for which you are applying. See the descriptions below to help determine which type you fall into.\nRegular Membership: \nAny North American firm or corporation or North American branch of an international firm or corporation shall be eligible for Regular Membership in the Institute which:\nManufactures precision mechanical springs with a majority of its production sold to unrelated companies. An unrelated company is defined as any firm holding less than 40% ownership, either directly or indirectly through a holding company, in the springmaking company.\nHas a reputation for business integrity and sound character; and\nMeets such other uniform requirements as may be established by the board of directors.\nHas its principal locations and principal operations in North America\nAssociate Membership:\nAny firm or corporation shall be eligible for Associate Membership in the Institute which:\nSupplies directly to firms or corporations eligible for Regular Membership materials, equipment or services, provided such materials, equipment or services are either incorporated in the finished spring product or are used directly in the manufacture and/or design of such product;\nHas a reputation for business integrity and sound character; and\nMeets such other uniform requirements as may be established by the board of directors.\nJoin Now\n Home\nAbout\nMember Benefits\nSprings Magazine\nOnline Store\nMembership\nLogin\n PO Box 5668 | Elgin, Illinois 60121 USA | Phone (847) 450-6848",
