      "text": "Gary McCoy, Executive Director – SMI\n Contact Us\n Contact Us\n Sign In\n Register\n Home\nAbout\n President’s Message\n Executive Officers and Board\n Past Presidents\n Staff List\n Privacy Policy\nMember Benefits\n Affinity Programs\n SMI Scholarship Program\n Springs Advice\n Regulatory Compliance\n Find a Springmaker\n Find a Supplier\nIssues\nSprings Magazine\n Issues\n Springs Magazine Media Kit\n Space Reservation Request\n Ad Submission\n Editorial Submission\nEvents\n Event Calendar\n Spring Design Training Program\n Annual Meeting\n SpringWorld\nOnline Store\nMembership\n Benefits of Membership\n Member Search\n Apply For Membership\n My account\nLogin\n Serving, supporting and educating North American precision spring manufacturers in their pursuit of competitiveness in world markets.\n Member Login\n Home\nAbout\n President’s Message\n Executive Officers and Board\n Past Presidents\n Staff List\n Privacy Policy\nMember Benefits\n Affinity Programs\n SMI Scholarship Program\n Springs Advice\n Regulatory Compliance\n Find a Springmaker\n Find a Supplier\nIssues\nSprings Magazine\n Issues\n Springs Magazine Media Kit\n Space Reservation Request\n Ad Submission\n Editorial Submission\nEvents\n Event Calendar\n Spring Design Training Program\n Annual Meeting\n SpringWorld\nOnline Store\nMembership\n Benefits of Membership\n Member Search\n Apply For Membership\n My account\nLogin\n Gary McCoy, Executive Director\n Job Title: Executive Director\n Email: gary@smihq.org\n Phone: 847-450-6240\n Gary McCoy oversees the operations of SMI as the association’s executive director. He served as managing editor of Springs magazine from 2008 to 2023 and has more than 30 years of experience in marketing communications, public relations and association management. Gary started Fairway Communications in Elgin, Illinois in 2000 and ran his own marketing communications business until 2022 when he left to join SMI. Previously, he was the director of communications for the Automotive Service Industry Association and a former president of the Automotive Communications Council. He earned a B.A. degree in Journalism and Mass Communications from Iowa State University and holds the professional development designation of Master Automotive Aftermarket Professional (MAAP) from the University of the Aftermarket.\n Home\nAbout\nMember Benefits\nSprings Magazine\nOnline Store\nMembership\nLogin\n PO Box 5668 | Elgin, Illinois 60121 USA | Phone (847) 450-6848",
